If you still get errors, you can remove the `broadcast_in_dim` for scalar-to-vector and just use the scalar directly in elementwise ops, as StableHLO will broadcast scalars automatically.  
If you want to be explicit, you can use `stablehlo.broadcast_in_dim` with `broadcast_dimensions = array<i64: >` for (f32) -> (16xf32), and `broadcast_dimensions = array<i64: 0>` for (16xf32) -> (16x16xf32) along batch, and `broadcast_dimensions = array<i64: 1>` for (16xf32) -> (16x16xf32) along channel.  
This program uses the explicit form.

